   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.4. Increased capacity of Member States to promote peaceful, stable and resilient societies through decent work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Sierra Leone, through its tripartite partners and local community-based organizations have engaged communities in Western Area, to reduce conflicts related to water-scarcity, and engaged community members for promotion of peaceful co-existence.

The West Africa Network for Peace Building (WANEP) conducted a Peace and Conflict Analysis from August to November 2022  in targeted communities, to identify conflict drivers, leading to the design of activities to address issues identified. This was also followed by a Water Value Chain Assessment, to assess decent work opportunities along the water value chain.
 The ILO trained the Sierra Leone Labour Congress and WANEP in October 2022, to implement activities highlighted. The ILO also provided technical guidance a by reviewing the TOR in July 2022 and draft reports (in October 2022) with follow-up virtual meetings throughout the implementation.</narrative>
   </description>
